WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.038 --> 00:00:06.542
It's been a pretty heavy duty winter
for us.

00:00:06.542 --> 00:00:08.978
It's been a little rough.

00:00:08.978 --> 00:00:10.112
Whoa!

00:00:10.179 --> 00:00:12.348
You know, just staying at home
and maintaining the farm.

00:00:12.781 --> 00:00:15.584
Go, go, go, go. No!

00:00:16.452 --> 00:00:17.653
The kids are kind of antsy

00:00:18.754 --> 00:00:20.923
if they're cooped up for too long.

00:00:20.923 --> 00:00:23.292
We're missing a chicken. I only count 29.

00:00:23.659 --> 00:00:27.796
So it's important getting them out and
having a change of pace for a little bit.

00:00:28.864 --> 00:00:30.065
There you go.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.003
Just being on the farm all winter long,

00:00:34.236 --> 00:00:39.575
we have been kind of cyclic
through these similar red meat cows.

00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:41.243
And chickens and all that.

00:00:41.243 --> 00:00:43.912
So it'd be nice to get out
and kind of change up the diet

00:00:43.912 --> 00:00:45.180
a little bit.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:51.553
Fish provides nutrients
that we can't get from our other animals.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.890
And we've been in Alaska
for a whole year now.

00:00:55.024 --> 00:00:59.895
So for the first time, we are going
to Mineral Lake to go ice fishing.

00:01:01.363 --> 00:01:01.897
Moses.

00:01:01.897 --> 00:01:02.531
Olivia.

00:01:02.531 --> 00:01:05.567
Come on, come on.

00:01:10.839 --> 00:01:12.875
Oh, he's on the way.

00:01:13.742 --> 00:01:14.343
All right.

00:01:15.944 --> 00:01:18.213
That's probably far enough
before we check the ice.

00:01:19.415 --> 00:01:21.350
I don't want you going out
before I check the thickness.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.119
I want to make sure it's safe.

00:01:34.096 --> 00:01:36.198
But should it be okay

00:01:36.198 --> 00:01:38.700
enough for us to be scooting across.

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:41.503
C'mon babies.

00:01:42.271 --> 00:01:44.840
With everything that we've had to do this

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:48.010
winter, we've had next to no free time.

00:01:48.644 --> 00:01:52.147
So having the opportunity to go out
and do something as a family

00:01:52.781 --> 00:01:55.017
is just such a blessing.

00:01:55.818 --> 00:01:57.953
I think I want to stop here.

00:01:57.953 --> 00:01:59.988
I think this looks fine.

00:02:01.857 --> 00:02:05.227
We're going to check
and see how deep it is.

00:02:14.369 --> 00:02:15.370
Did you hit water?

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:16.572
I think I did.

00:02:17.639 --> 00:02:19.942
I'm goinna check.

00:02:20.642 --> 00:02:21.877
No, we're still at ice.

00:02:22.211 --> 00:02:23.479
Whaaat!.

00:02:24.413 --> 00:02:28.150
So the trick is to try the extension here
to see if that's any good

00:02:31.687 --> 00:02:34.356
Oh, yeah.

00:02:36.225 --> 00:02:37.693
Pull her up.

00:02:38.393 --> 00:02:40.929
Just a little funky.

00:02:48.036 --> 00:02:48.570
Oh, my gosh,

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:51.640
it's still not even touching water.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.775
I'm wondering
if we're not hitting ground or something.

00:02:59.448 --> 00:03:02.351
Is that like tar, flakes, stuff?

00:03:03.485 --> 00:03:06.221
Either that or weeds or something.

00:03:06.221 --> 00:03:06.922
All right.

00:03:08.023 --> 00:03:10.792
Hole number two and move on.

00:03:11.493 --> 00:03:13.362
All right, follow dad.

00:03:13.428 --> 00:03:15.197
Hopefully we get lucky.

